{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' /local/home/scheschb/.codex/plugins/cache/aim/AmazonBuilderCoreAIAgents-core/1.0.6507655022/skills/brazil-build-analyzer-skill/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: brazil-build-analyzer-skill\ndescription: Runs brazil-build with reliable log capture for agent inspection. Use when building packages, diagnosing build failures, or running tests in local Brazil workspaces.\nversion: 1.1.0\ntags: [skill, brazil, build, analyzer, failure, diagnosis, troubleshooting]\n---\n\n# Brazil Build Analyzer Skill\n\nUse the bundled wrapper instead of invoking `brazil-build` directly. It\nvalidates the package context, captures complete build output in a file, and\npreserves the build's exit status.\n\n(Codex-only) When sandboxing is active, run both scripts with elevated sandbox\npermissions on every invocation; do not attempt them inside the sandbox first.\n\nRun the bundled [run-build-workflow.sh](scripts/run-build-workflow.sh) with the\npackage directory as the command working directory. With no arguments it runs\n`brazil-build release`; otherwise pass the requested `brazil-build` arguments\ndirectly.\n\nRun the wrapper directly; MUST NOT pipe or redirect its output through `tail`,\n`grep`, or another command.\n\nAfter the build, the wrapper prints the last 20 log lines followed by the final\nstatus, exit code, and absolute path to the build log. This log file can be\ngrepped if the relevant information is not towards the end of the build output.\n\nTo run the build _and_ grep the output in a single shell invocation, use\n[replay-last-build.sh](scripts/replay-last-build.sh), e.g.:\n\n```bash\nrun-build-workflow.sh ; replay-last-build.sh | grep -i -e failure -e error -e success\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
