{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_112","type":"agent_message","text":"I found the BLAKE primitive defect: the C code increments the high bit counter only when the wrapped low counter becomes exactly zero, not on every unsigned carry. My first Rust translation used normal carry propagation, which agrees for empty input but diverges for non-empty messages. I’m correcting that deliberate C behavior now."}}
